id:                     E507
trigger_tool: cmake|clang++|gcc
phase: configuration|compilation
error_signature: sp_thread_sleep.*pthread_setcancelstate|pthread_setcancelstate.*undeclared
severity: 3
category:               cmake, boost, capability-detection, pthread
match_keywords: pthread_setcancelstate, CheckCXXSymbolExists, Threads::Threads, BOOST_SP_THREAD_SLEEP_NO_PTHREAD_SETCANCELSTATE, KWStyle
title: Probe optional pthread cancellation state before enabling Boost sleep calls
root_cause: POSIX thread support does not guarantee the optional pthread cancellation-state API, while bundled Boost can infer its call path from BOOST_HAS_PTHREADS alone.
affected_scope: CMake projects that embed Boost thread-sleep code on POSIX-capable targets without pthread_setcancelstate.
verification_cmd: Configure and build twice with a link-aware pthread_setcancelstate probe forced absent and present; require the guard only in the absent build and scan out platform-name conditionals.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: link-aware-symbol-capability-selection
rec_description: Probe pthread_setcancelstate with Threads::Threads and apply BOOST_SP_THREAD_SLEEP_NO_PTHREAD_SETCANCELSTATE only to the target that embeds the Boost sleep implementation when the symbol is unavailable.
rec_command: Use CheckCXXSymbolExists with CMAKE_REQUIRED_LIBRARIES=Threads::Threads, restore the probe state, and gate only the cancellation-state calls while retaining nanosleep.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: cmake-target-compile-definition
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach:
fallback_description:
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl:
forbid_1_pattern: __OHOS__|HarmonyOS|pthread_setcancelstate.*stub
forbid_1_reason: Platform-name branches and no-op pthread stubs misrepresent the target capability and can alter thread cancellation semantics.
forbid_1_consequence: The adaptation becomes non-portable or silently changes runtime behavior.
principles:
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: [E127]
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
